## Code Style Guidelines

### Kotlin Conventions
- Use `val` over `var` whenever possible
- Prefer data classes for model objects
- Use sealed classes for state management
- Implement null safety properly
- Use extension functions for utility methods
- Follow Kotlin naming conventions (camelCase for functions/variables, PascalCase for classes)

### Android Best Practices
- Always use ViewBinding instead of findViewById
- Implement proper lifecycle management
- Handle configuration changes correctly
- Use string resources for all user-facing text
- Implement proper error handling with try-catch blocks
- Check permissions before accessing protected features
- Use Timber for logging in debug builds

### MVVM Architecture Rules
- ViewModels should not reference Views or Context (except ApplicationContext)
- Use LiveData or StateFlow for UI state observation
- Repository pattern for data operations
- Single source of truth principle
- Separation of concerns between layers

## Key Components Implementation

### 1. BatteryMonitorService
- Must be a Foreground Service for Android 8.0+
- Show persistent notification while monitoring
- Handle Doze mode and App Standby
- Implement proper service lifecycle
- Use WakeLock if necessary

### 2. BatteryBroadcastReceiver
- Register for ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED
- Filter for charging state changes
- Check battery level against threshold
- Trigger notification only when charging

### 3. Notification System
- Create NotificationChannel for Android O+
- Set proper notification priority (HIGH/MAX)
- Use custom sound with looping
- Implement dismiss and snooze actions
- Handle Do Not Disturb mode

